    explanation: "- EventBridge routes events by content. A rule is a JSON pattern: nested objects must match structurally, arrays are lists of alternatives, and content filters such as numeric and prefix live inside those arrays\n- Step Functions runs a state machine written in Amazon States Language. Retry is configured per state, Catch routes failures to a compensating state, and the execution history shows every transition\n- Because Retry lives inside a state, a flaky step is re-attempted without re-running the states that already succeeded — which is what stops a retried reservation from charging a card twice\n- SQS is a queue: one message, one successful consumer, at-least-once delivery, so consumers must be idempotent. SNS is fan-out: one publish reaches every subscriber independently\n- Kinesis Data Streams keeps records ordered within a shard and retains them for replay, so several independent consumers can read the same stream at their own pace\n- A Lambda consumer of Kinesis or SQS should return batchItemFailures rather than throwing, so only the failed records are redelivered instead of the whole batch\n- The strongest default is: EventBridge to decouple producers from consumers, Step Functions when the work has steps that can fail independently",
