    explanation: "- ECR is a private registry with scan-on-push, immutable tag settings and lifecycle policies that expire untagged layers\n- An image has two names: a tag, which can be moved, and a digest, which cannot. Only the digest identifies specific bytes, so it is the only safe reference for a deployment\n- CodeBuild runs a buildspec and authenticates to ECR with the build role's short-lived credentials rather than a stored password\n- Reading the digest back from ECR after the push — rather than computing it locally — is what makes a later promotion check meaningful\n- An ECS task definition has two distinct roles: the execution role pulls the image and writes logs, the task role is what your application code receives. Sharing one hands application code the registry permissions\n- Secrets belong in the task definition's secrets block, fetched by the agent at start, not in environment, which is visible in plain text in the console and API\n- App Runner trades control for simplicity: point it at an image or a repository and it handles the load balancer, TLS and scaling. ECS on Fargate is the middle ground, EKS the most control\n- A container health check tells the scheduler that the service can answer, which is different from the process still running",
